INT. HIGH SCHOOL GYM - WRESTLING MAT - EVENING

Bleachers half-full. A banner reading STATE SEMIFINAL sags from the rafters. Two boys in singlets circle on a faded blue mat.

COACH DELACROIX, fifties, stands at the edge in a windbreaker, arms folded. REFEREE BOHDAN, sixties, crouches nearby with a whistle in his teeth. On the mat, HUGO ABERNATHY, seventeen, red singlet, and KARIM SZYMANSKI, seventeen, blue, lock hands.

He drops low. He shoots. He grabs a leg and drives. The other boy sprawls and rolls, and he scrambles to his knees and goes for the half nelson, and for a second they are one tangle of limbs and sweat.

COACH DELACROIX
(to the whole gym)
Stay off his hips!

REFEREE BOHDAN
(to Hugo)
Watch your hands.

KARIM
(muttering to himself)
Come on, come on...

The whistle shrieks. They break. The gym holds its breath. Referee Bohdan points to the blue boy.

REFEREE BOHDAN (CONT'D)
Two points.

He gets up slowly. He looks at the scoreboard. Looks at his coach. Shakes out his arms and lowers himself back into a stance, and across from him the other boy exhales, long and loud, and settles in.

COACH DELACROIX
(low)
You're fine. You're fine.
